B.M4=s(["Own Flutter development for internal enterprise applications used by ZATCA staff and field teams, including the ZAKATY Zakat calculator and the Fahes field inspection system, within a government environment with strict security and delivery requirements.","Migrated ZAKATY from Flutter 2.x to Flutter 3.24 and re-architected it on Clean Architecture with BLoC/Cubit, go_router, GetIt/injectable, and freezed, establishing a modular, testable codebase with improved maintainability and runtime performance.","Delivered cross-platform features for the public ZATCA app across .NET MAUI/C# and React Native/TypeScript: customs declaration and tax-service flows, bilingual Arabic/English journeys, navigation, and reusable components, including an internal C# port of mk_smart_search and centralized SAR currency display.","Core contributor (150+ commits) to ZATCA Mobile, the React Native / Expo rewrite of the public app: signup journeys (establishment, individual, GCC resident), Nafath / Ping Identity authentication, service favourites, and RTL flows on a feature-based Clean Architecture with tsyringe DI and TanStack Query.","Integrated F5 security, Dynatrace monitoring, and Firebase Analytics across mobile apps to meet ZATCA security, reliability, and observability requirements for production government services.","Mentor 2 junior Flutter developers through code reviews and pair programming; defined shared widget and architecture conventions now adopted across team projects.","Introduced AI-assisted engineering to the team, including AI coding agents, code-intelligence tooling, and agent skills, and presented practical agentic workflows in an internal Innovation Team talk."],t.s)
